      "text": "The temperature is 77 degrees whenever $-t^2 +12t+50 =77$, which is equivalent to $t^2-12t+27=0$. We can factor the equation as $(t-3)(t-9)=0$, so the solutions are $t=3$ and $t=9$. However, $t=9$ cannot be a valid solution since $-t^2+12t+50$ is defined for only nonnegative values of $t$ and in this case, the temperature is negative at $t=9$. Hence our only solution in this case is $t=3$.",
